Parser
------

Parser:
	Pros and cons
	Generic:
		+ modify grammar file, no code change
		+ can do grammar validation
		- C++ data based grammar not trivial
		- not flexible grammar
		- automatic error making (not always clear)
		- automatic parse tree has to be converted again later
	Custom:
		- more to type
		- more changes to make manually if grammar changes
		+ custom diagnostics
		+ custom grammar adjustments for non LL(1)
		+ direct "final" ast building
		+ slightly faster
	
	Parser is an external object that builds ast components from the outside and assembles them together. AST objects have only introspection stuff mostly. They lose most of the concrete syntax, retain only SourcePos'es for diagnostics.
	AST objects are as simple as possible. Avoid data replication, prefer algorithmic lookup instead (optimise later).
	eg: types are directly internized and have no parse tree equivalent (position is kept by enclosing member/argument declaration if needed), binary operations are derivated from method call directly

Type
	ValueType (enum num, bool, text, data, opaque)
	ObjectType
